KuberNow - Privacy Policy
Effective date: November 11, 2026

1. Scope and contact
This policy describes how KuberNow ("we," "us," or "our") handles personal information in its financial education application, website, and related services (the "Service"), including KuberNow: My Money Journey.
Contact for privacy questions and requests: Amit@AmericaMaGujarati.com.

2. Information you provide
Depending on the features available and used, information we receive may include:
- Account details such as your name, email, sign-in identifier, and language preferences.
- Financial estimates you choose to submit, such as income, expenses, assets, debts, savings, goals, and calculator assumptions.
- Learning progress, answers, saved tasks, and preferences.
- Messages, feedback, and support correspondence.
- Purchase status and transaction identifiers when paid features are offered. Payment information is handled under the payment provider's or app store's own privacy practices.
These categories apply only when the corresponding feature is offered and you use it. You may use estimates instead of exact financial amounts. Do not submit bank passwords, Social Security numbers, full payment-card details, or unnecessary sensitive information through educational inputs or support.

3. Technical information
Online features may process IP addresses, device and operating-system information, app versions, timestamps, error reports, and usage activity to deliver, maintain, and secure the Service. Cookies, local storage, and similar technologies may support sign-in, preferences, or usage measurement where implemented.
Browser and device settings control some storage, permissions, and notifications. Disabling them may affect functionality. Information stored only on your device is not received by us unless you submit or synchronize it through a Service feature. Uninstalling does not necessarily delete information previously submitted to an account.

4. Purposes
We use relevant information to provide accounts, learning content, saved progress, tasks, and calculations; display educational examples using your inputs; respond to support requests; communicate service updates; maintain reliability and prevent abuse; manage purchases where offered; and meet legal obligations.
Optional marketing messages, where offered, include an unsubscribe method. Device notifications can be managed in device settings.

5. Sharing
We may use providers for hosting, authentication, storage, diagnostics, communications, and payment processing, to the extent those functions are used. Information necessary for their work may be shared subject to applicable safeguards.
We may disclose information to comply with law or valid legal process, investigate fraud or security incidents, or protect rights and safety. Information may transfer in a merger, acquisition, or sale of the relevant business, subject to applicable law and notice requirements.
We do not sell personal financial inputs or share them for targeted advertising. Materially different uses or sharing will be addressed through an updated policy and notice or consent where required.

6. Retention and security
We retain information for the purposes described here, considering account activity, support needs, information sensitivity, and legal obligations. Information is deleted or de-identified when no longer needed, subject to lawful retention exceptions. Backup copies may remain until overwritten or removed.
We use reasonable safeguards appropriate to the information processed. No internet transmission or storage method is completely secure.

7. Access, correction, and deletion
Email Amit@AmericaMaGujarati.com from your account email to request access, correction, deletion of particular information, or deletion of your account and associated data. Explain your request. We may verify identity before responding.
Depending on applicable law, you may also have rights to portability, restriction, objection, withdrawal of consent, or appeal, and to contact a privacy regulator. We respond as required by applicable law. Legal, transaction, security, or fraud-prevention records may be retained where permitted; we will explain relevant exceptions.
Account deletion and uninstalling do not automatically cancel subscriptions. Cancel through the billing provider or app store.

8. International processing
Information may be processed in the United States and other countries where the Service or its providers operate. Laws may differ. Where international transfers require safeguards, we will use those required by applicable law.

9. Adults and third-party services
The Service is intended for adults 18 and older. Contact us if you believe a child has submitted personal information so we can investigate and remove it as appropriate.
External websites, stores, sign-in providers, and payment services have their own privacy policies. Viewing this policy on GitHub is also subject to GitHub's privacy practices.

10. Updates
We may update this policy and its effective date. Material changes will be communicated through the Service or another appropriate channel, with notice or consent where required.

